      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Right, right, right, a temp spike in the reefer unit, you say? Well, first things first, we need to cool things down, pronto! It's like when the little green goblins decide to throw a surprise party in the middle of winter – you gotta cool it down before things get too wild. So, let's get those fans whirring and maybe even consider a temporary cold bath in a nearby ice bath, if you have one handy. \n\nNow, about checking if the batch is still safe to sell, well, that's a bit like trying to figure out if the goblins have stolen your grandma's secret pie recipe – you need to check the quality. Look at the fish's color, smell, and texture. If it's still looking like a fresh catch of the day, then it's probably still good to go. But if it's looking more like a goblin's dinner, then it's time to call it a day and let the fish go to waste. \n\nAnd remember, always keep an eye on the temperature – it's like keeping an eye on those pesky goblins. If things start to heat up again, you might need to consider a more drastic cooling method, like a blast freezer or even a quick dip in liquid",
